3d12577"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Ahn Seung-ho, better known as Tony An, is a South Korean singer-songwriter, best known as a member of boy band H.O.T. After H.O.T. disbanded in 2001, its ex-members Tony An, Jang Woo-hyuk and Lee Jae-won formed the dance music trio jtL. Eventually, JTL unofficially disbanded as each member, including An, released their solo material.","title":"Tony An","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tony_An"}},"Q484027":{"id":"Q484027","name":"Joo","ko":"JOO","birthName":"Jung Min-joo","birthNameEn":"Jung Min-joo","aliases":["Jung Min-joo"],"birth":"1990-10-11","death":"","birthplace":"Mapo District","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor"],"debut":"2008","agencies":[{"name":"JYP Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483238","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Woollim Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q50596","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/superminjoo/","x":"https://x.com/JOOt_aime","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC_CKYTfg7WYqOAFqnZ5b2Rw","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/39f5795e-b23a-454f-b1e2-e064bd4cf47b"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Jung Min-joo, born Jung A-rin and known professionally as Joo (stylized in all caps), is a South Korean singer, songwriter and musical actress. In 2006, she became a contestant on JYP Entertainment's Superstar Survival. Although she didn't win, she was accepted as a trainee at JYP Entertainment. After two years of training, Joo debuted as a soloist with her single album Young Girl in January 2008. However, she resumed training for two years, as she didn't feel ready for her debut. Joo later returned in January 2011 by releasing her EP Heartmade.","title":"Joo (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joo_%28singer%29"}},"Q491515":{"id":"Q491515","name":"Nana","ko":"나나","birthName":"임진아","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Im Jin-a","Im Jin-ah"],"birth":"1991-09-14","death":"","birthplace":"Cheongju","natio